stage.001.title = Fourth Wall

stage.001.description = Your first real project: building the fourth wall of a room.

stage.001.dialogue.intro = Hello, Engineer! Your first project is ready. I want you to build the fourth wall of this room for me.

stage.001.dialogue.instruction = Before you even pick up a single brick, you must calculate the exact number of bricks needed. The budget is limited.

stage.001.dialogue.warning = Remember, more bricks do not necessarily mean better construction. The project must be built exactly according to the blueprint and contract.

stage.001.dialogue.math_complete = Calculations confirmed. You can now procure the required materials.

stage.001.dialogue.collapse = The wall was unstable. Check your calculations and the way the bricks were placed again.

stage.001.dialogue.success = Excellent! The fourth wall has been successfully built and tested. You have successfully completed and delivered your first project.

stage.001.question = How many bricks are needed to build the fourth wall?

stage.001.hint.01 = First, calculate how many half-meter bricks fit along the 4-meter length of the wall.

stage.001.hint.02 = Then multiply the number of bricks in each row by the number of rows in the wall.

stage.001.solution = To build the wall, first divide its length by the length of each brick to determine the number of bricks in each row. Then divide the height of the wall by the height of each brick to determine the number of rows. Finally, multiply the number of bricks in each row by the number of rows.